course: dictionary
lesson: 2792
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbered senses, and the words around the word show you which one the writer means. The word disorder has three main meanings: a mess, trouble in public, and an illness.
explain: «The bedroom was in disorder after the party.» The clues are the party and the mess. Things are not in their places, so disorder means an untidy state.
explain: «A sleep disorder can stop the body working normally.» Here the clue is the body. A disorder is a condition that stops the body or mind working as it should, so this is an illness.
explain: «When gaming takes over life and someone cannot stop even when they want to, it is worth talking about; doctors recognise "gaming disorder" in serious cases.» The clues are doctors and serious cases, so this is a health condition, not a mess. Try the everyday meaning in the sentence. If it does not fit, the word must mean something else.
fact: Disorder is a noun, so you can say a disorder or disorders.
fact: «Disorder» can mean a mess, where things are not in order.
fact: «Public disorder» means trouble or fighting among people in public.
fact: «A disorder» can also mean an illness or condition that stops the body or mind working normally, such as «an eating disorder».
fact: «Gaming disorder» is a condition that doctors recognise in serious cases, and it can affect children as well as adults. People with disorders deserve kindness and proper help.
exercise: «The toys were in disorder all over the classroom floor.» What does in disorder mean here? | A special kind of game | *A messy state, with things out of place | Very quiet and calm | Shiny and new
exercise: «Police dealt with public disorder outside the stadium.» What is public disorder? | A kind of school lesson | A public park with lots of trees | *Trouble or fighting among people in public | A quiet, orderly queue
exercise: «Doctors recognise "gaming disorder" in serious cases.» What kind of disorder is meant here? | *A medical condition that affects the body or mind | A mess in a bedroom | A type of sports tournament | A loud argument at school
test: «He has a sleep disorder, so he sees a doctor.» What does disorder mean in this sentence? | Trouble in public | *An illness or condition that stops normal working | An untidy bedroom | A loud noise at night
test: Which phrase means trouble or fighting among people in public? | a sleep disorder | tidy room | in disorder | *public disorder
exam: Which meaning of disorder fits best in «Gaming disorder is worth talking about if it takes over life»? | A loud, cheerful game | A mess or untidy state | *A health condition of the mind or body | Trouble among a crowd
